.SH NAME
anpu-tools-verify - Audit installed tool binaries against their install-time digests


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu tools verify [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Re-hash every installed registry binary and compare it with the
sha256 recorded when 'anpu tools install' put it on disk. Any binary that
changed since install is reported as drift — ANPU refuses to execute such
binaries at run time until you audit the host and reinstall
('anpu tools install  --force') to re-baseline.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for verify


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


